Hmmm... there are quite a few things wrong with this. First, the
probability of
shop items is separate from the probability of random items (shknam.c
vs. objects.c).
In shknam.c, magic lamps are given a probability of 3% per item
generated in a
lighting shop. As for hardware stores, they just generate a random
item of type
TOOL_CLASS... nowhere else in the game is a "light source" generated
specifically.
Of tool items, magic lamps have a 1.5% chance of being generated. Then
of course
there is the issue of mimics taking up space in the shops, or the
issue of shops not
being generated in a given minetown (Izchak's always is, but hardware
stores aren't
necessarily). Finally, taking the probability for generation in the
lighting store
and just adding the probability for generation in the hardware store
is... well,
really bad math, and doesn't really make sense at all. I would put the
overall
probability at 20% at an absolute maximum... probably closer to 15% or
so.

